Z||000000||Formula 18||06-12-2001||12:42 AM||||Probally one of the most asked question on the board but will 15x6.5 in., 5 lug, 100mm bolt pattern with 38 mm offset work on an 88 formula??? <P><BR>They have Dunlop SP Sport 4000 A/S P195/60/R15 on 'em.. I'll probally have to change them rihgt? <P>What would you pay fot these?? <A HREF="http://www.aaarims.com/wheels/69387.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aaarims.com/wheels/69387.JPG</A> <P>Thanks,<BR>Brian<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||06-12-2001||01:45 AM||||Not 100% sure about the offset, but I'm gonna say they will work. I know the 5 lug, 5x100 will work.<P>And as far as changing the tires, I wouldn't see why unless you just want to. I've got a set of 225/50/15s on an 88 coupe out here. They fit fine. <P>I think the 195/60/15s or 215/60/15s were stock on 88 Formulas and GT<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||06-12-2001||08:29 AM||||Yes they fit. But why would you want to put a smaller rim in a Formula? Stock rears are 7". It would not look good. Also 195 tires are way to thin for me. But if you like them is your decision.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||06-12-2001||01:52 PM||||88 Formula/GT: <BR>Front: 205/60-15 on 15x6" wheels<BR>Rear: 215/60-15 on 15x7" wheels  <BR>Not sure about the offset, but 38 sounds close enough.  I believe it's about 42mm?  I've heard of people using 45mm offset without problems.||||reg||1
